1
00:01:49,760 --> 00:02:09,090
 mississippi orland declared because it was the start of the 18th century before they had got that

2
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:16,420
 far in the south the comanches were fighting a bloody war against the spanish invaders out here

3
00:02:16,420 --> 00:02:22,370
 in the east skirmishes with the new arrivals and massacres went on pushing the indians toward the

4
00:02:22,370 --> 00:02:26,990
 west and that's what happened to the blackfoot tribe and the cheyenne and the sioux and many

5
00:02:26,990 --> 00:02:47,120
 others until on these vast plains no white men no horses no firearms like this for long we're

6
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:49,720
 We're marching to the rivers where we can hunt buffalo.

7
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:51,520
 And will you let me hunt with you?

8
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:54,050
 You're too small now, later when you're grown up.

9
00:02:54,050 --> 00:03:15,560
 Possessions, go to your mom.

10
00:03:15,560 --> 00:03:17,440
 Which animals they're riding?

11
00:03:17,440 --> 00:03:24,470
 No, never saw them before.

12
00:03:24,470 --> 00:04:09,260
 Seems to be a friend of man, so it must be a dog.

13
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:13,230
 It's a big dog, it's good to eat.

14
00:04:13,230 --> 00:04:15,280
 I wouldn't be surprised.

15
00:04:15,280 --> 00:04:17,280
 Good meat, you can tell, touch it.

16
00:04:17,280 --> 00:04:25,330
 It's not a buffalo.

17
00:04:25,330 --> 00:04:31,380
 Didn't do too badly, did we?

18
00:04:31,380 --> 00:04:34,810
 Guess not, they didn't steal much, and we got good meat.

19
00:04:34,810 --> 00:04:42,280
 Thinking, with these big dogs, if we had some, it would change quite a lot, eh?

20
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:44,180
 Hmm, yes.

21
00:04:45,530 --> 00:04:51,730
 Signal means danger.

22
00:04:53,280 --> 00:04:56,250
 Think we're going to attack them.

23
00:04:57,600 --> 00:05:01,770
 In fact, we come as friends, and it would be a lot better to tell them.

24
00:05:19,260 --> 00:05:31,360
 It's all right.

25
00:05:32,210 --> 00:05:34,660
 Coming, guys, we can go to see them.

26
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:14,730
 See you the same color.

27
00:06:16,620 --> 00:06:20,980
 That's it. We are friendly Indians.

28
00:06:21,780 --> 00:06:24,770
 These ceremonial positions, I'm getting too old.

29
00:06:29,150 --> 00:06:35,020
 Badly loaded my peace pipe.

30
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:38,040
 Now how can we have a decent powwow with a pipe like this?

31
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:41,160
 Why didn't you tell me there was no tobacco over my pipe?

32
00:06:48,330 --> 00:06:56,190
 It's a real calumet.

33
00:06:56,610 --> 00:06:59,230
 We were attacked by Apaches.

34
00:07:00,610 --> 00:07:01,730
 They were on ponies.

35
00:07:02,350 --> 00:07:03,830
 It was a ferocious attack.

36
00:07:05,680 --> 00:07:07,810
 That makes you angry, eh?

37
00:07:07,850 --> 00:07:09,090
 Well, that's what it did to us.

38
00:07:10,150 --> 00:07:11,790
 Now, let's talk business, all right?

39
00:07:12,950 --> 00:07:13,350
 Buffalos.

40
00:07:13,490 --> 00:07:14,750
 Have you seen any buffalos around?

41
00:07:16,890 --> 00:07:20,310
 West, north, south?

42
00:07:20,390 --> 00:07:22,130
 No, well, would you like to trade a little?

43
00:07:22,710 --> 00:07:56,630
 You're an Indian, and don't you forget I won't trade.

44
00:07:56,950 --> 00:07:58,220
 I'm keeping that one.

45
00:07:58,730 --> 00:07:59,340
 Wrap it up.

46
00:07:59,490 --> 00:08:00,190
 I'll take it home.

47
00:08:54,210 --> 00:09:48,420
 Buffalo.

48
00:09:48,820 --> 00:09:53,130
 Good news, it's lots of them.

49
00:10:09,060 --> 00:10:22,980
 Remember, when you hunt, it's not for your own glory to be above the other.

50
00:10:22,980 --> 00:10:31,910
 When you hunt your belly together, little chief, as it happens, I am that chief.

51
00:10:32,300 --> 00:10:38,120
 And if you don't obey, you'll be, he said it.

52
00:10:38,910 --> 00:10:41,900
 I want you to kill the number we need, no more.

53
00:10:42,140 --> 00:10:45,610
 Remember that every one of you, be what we need.

54
00:12:49,890 --> 00:13:48,210
 In a word, every big dog will be sitting pretty.

55
00:13:54,590 --> 00:14:00,210
 Here, children, over here.

56
00:14:01,790 --> 00:14:04,470
 Now, I'm going to show you something that's going to surprise you.

57
00:14:04,830 --> 00:14:06,590
 You remember those eagles that you caught?

58
00:14:06,690 --> 00:14:09,570
 Well, when you're warriors, you learn the right to wear certain feathers.

59
00:14:09,570 --> 00:14:14,140
 Now, if you strike an enemy, or if you are wounded, once or several times,

60
00:14:14,420 --> 00:14:18,280
 Another one if you kill an enemy, and especially one if you scalped one.

61
00:14:18,630 --> 00:14:21,890
 Yes, but we're already grown up, and they won't let us be warriors.

62
00:14:22,370 --> 00:14:24,790
 That's right. They won't even let us hunt with them.

63
00:14:25,330 --> 00:14:26,630
 And we're good hunters.

64
00:14:26,970 --> 00:14:28,590
 Now, now, patience, little ones.

65
00:14:28,630 --> 00:14:31,090
 You have to learn patience, and you'll become hunters pretty soon.

66
00:14:31,090 --> 00:14:38,050
 But first, you must submit to certain trials, fasting, sweating, to purify your body and your mind.

67
00:14:38,620 --> 00:14:43,640
 No, you go in search of the great mysterious spirit first and all the power that will help you.

68
00:14:53,440 --> 00:15:38,940
 The eyes of the heart seek sacred contact with you.

69
00:15:39,950 --> 00:15:42,880
 To generations, heed their all greater glory.

70
00:16:28,660 --> 00:16:29,580
 A very good sign.

71
00:16:29,700 --> 00:16:31,080
 You will be a great hunter.

72
00:16:32,980 --> 00:16:38,910
 There was a giant eagle protecting me, Mr. Hunter, my lad.

73
00:16:39,520 --> 00:16:41,070
 What I saw was a big snake.

74
00:16:41,190 --> 00:16:41,550
 I mean it.

75
00:16:41,590 --> 00:16:43,010
 It was easily this big.

76
00:16:43,150 --> 00:16:46,670
 In that case, fair play isn't going to be in your makeup.

77
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:47,940
 In yours, tell me.

78
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,100
 Snake, too, but a small one I saw.

79
00:16:50,180 --> 00:16:51,780
 Yeah, a tiny little one.

80
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:53,060
 It was about this big.

81
00:17:01,710 --> 00:17:02,730
 Wasn't a great big one.

82
00:17:03,090 --> 00:17:04,130
 A little one like that.

83
00:17:08,720 --> 00:17:09,640
 Oh, right.

84
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:14,150
 Tonight, you will come to my teepee and I will give you your protective charms.

85
00:17:14,150 --> 00:17:18,830
 There, now, each of you has his medicine charm, pebbles and healing herbs.

86
00:17:18,830 --> 00:17:21,750
 And you will get your feathers after you have earned them.

87
00:17:21,750 --> 00:17:24,730
 I'd like to know what's in your medicine bag.

88
00:17:24,730 --> 00:17:30,650
 My lad, I am the shaman and big chief, I am a healer, I am an astrologist and more.

89
00:17:30,650 --> 00:17:37,670
 Naturally, if I'm going to do all this, I need the tools of my trades to predict and cure and visit the spirits.

90
00:17:37,670 --> 00:17:42,920
 Now, all of you are men. Go out and dance with the other warriors.

91
00:17:42,920 --> 00:18:36,840
 I was absolutely sure the big dogs were going to return.

92
00:18:37,570 --> 00:18:40,770
 They, uh, trade things.

93
00:18:41,190 --> 00:18:49,600
 But why not in all your goods?

94
00:18:49,660 --> 00:19:31,500
 But I am interested in your big dog special.

95
00:19:32,050 --> 00:19:34,460
 Nobody right makes you ask me.

96
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:42,360
 I just wondered because, well, I think you're beautiful.

97
00:19:43,130 --> 00:19:45,480
 You like to be my squad, huh?

98
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:47,840
 Do you have any of those big dogs?

99
00:19:48,310 --> 00:19:49,390
 Ponies, we call them.

100
00:19:49,970 --> 00:19:52,670
 Why, no, as it happens, I haven't got any.

101
00:19:52,950 --> 00:19:54,490
 But I'm going to get some.

102
00:19:54,490 --> 00:19:54,990
 Huh?

103
00:19:58,100 --> 00:20:00,650
 Now, our big dogs are ponies.

104
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:03,560
 There are three, but the hunting season's approaching,

105
00:20:03,700 --> 00:20:05,560
 and for that, we'll need more of them.

106
00:20:05,720 --> 00:20:07,260
 Many more if we're to travel.

107
00:20:07,560 --> 00:20:10,730
 Now, in the village, it is said that the Poncas have ponies.

108
00:20:10,850 --> 00:20:12,130
 Four moons march from here.

109
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:15,100
 This can serve as an excellent trial for our young braves.

110
00:20:15,780 --> 00:20:18,650
 Near their mountain expedition, bringing ponies back.

111
00:20:18,650 --> 00:22:47,870
 Set off on a buffalo.

112
00:22:50,640 --> 00:22:53,090
 Hide well, or they're all strong.

113
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:56,270
 So, son, study them well.

114
00:22:57,540 --> 00:22:59,220
 If the one you've chosen runs straight,

115
00:22:59,420 --> 00:23:02,150
 you can go up close to him and kill him with your arrows.

116
00:23:03,720 --> 00:23:08,420
 Turns his head, looks at you from the corner of his eye.

117
00:23:08,820 --> 00:23:11,740
 Careful, he can turn on you, rip open your pony and kill you.

118
00:23:21,270 --> 00:23:24,310
 At last, ponies, wild ones, and I knew that one day we'd find them.

119
00:23:25,360 --> 00:23:28,500
 I knew that one day the great powers would send us ponies.

120
00:23:29,340 --> 00:23:44,420
 Now prove your men, braves, all of you. Come, friend.

121
00:23:44,650 --> 00:23:47,660
 Together we will capture the ponies for the glory of our tribe.

122
00:23:47,900 --> 00:23:50,970
 I will give you the finest eagle feather and the softest sap.

123
00:23:50,970 --> 00:24:30,160
 And the buffaloes are rare ponies, so now we can move much more easily.

124
00:24:30,660 --> 00:24:33,320
 In my opinion, we must migrate before winter.

125
00:24:34,260 --> 00:24:51,290
 What is this? Your face is pale. Are you sick or what?

126
00:24:51,780 --> 00:24:54,540
 Well, let's begin or else we'll never get started.

127
00:25:27,400 --> 00:25:34,480
 Rifles, whiskey, germs brought by the white man,

128
00:25:34,760 --> 00:25:37,490
 gifts to the Indians of the Great Plains, yes.

129
00:25:37,960 --> 00:25:40,140
 Yes, all this was to change their way of life.

130
00:25:40,560 --> 00:25:43,580
 The unstoppable steamroller, the white man's advance,

131
00:25:43,700 --> 00:25:46,220
 would soon chase the Indians from their lands.

132
00:25:46,490 --> 00:25:47,970
 Farther, always farther.

